\title{Comparison of Topologies}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    Let #{\tau_1} and #{\tau_2} be topologies on the same set #{X}. The
    topology #{\tau_1} is \strong{finer}, or \strong{stronger}, than
    #{\tau_2} if
    ##{
        \tau_2\subseteq\tau_1.
    }
    Equivalently, #{\tau_2} is \strong{coarser}, or \strong{weaker}, than
    #{\tau_1}. Thus a finer topology has more open sets and imposes a stronger
    continuity requirement on maps into the space.
}
